        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          OBJECTIVES:<br>
The middleware is an intelligent data management and communications software that facilitates the acquisition, integration, management, and distribution of data from on-orbit vehicle medical and environmental devices, sensors, and systems. The software reduces crew time and ensure the accuracy of data collection and timeliness of data delivery. 
<p>
The objectives of the Middleware were to: <ol>
<li>Reduce or eliminate the time required of an on-orbit crew and ground personnel [which include Surgeon, Biomedical Engineer (BME), and Medical Operations Data Specialist] to access, transfer, and manipulate medical data. 
<li>Support the integrated demonstration that the on-orbit crew has the ability to access medical data/information via an intuitive and crew-friendly solution to assist/aid in the treatment of a medical condition. 
<li>Develop a common data management framework and architecture that can be ubiquitously used to automate repetitive data collection, management, and communications tasks for all crew health and life sciences activities. 
<li>Ensure crew access to medical data during periods of reduced or unavailable ground communication. 
<li>Develop a common data management framework and architecture that allows for scalability, extensibility, and interoperability of data sources and data users. 
<li>Lower total cost of ownership for development and sustainment of peripheral hardware and software that utilize the Middleware for data management. 
<li>Provide better crew health via reduction in crew errors, crew time, and ground time.</ol>
<p>
APPROACH:<br>
The Exploration Medical System was designed to demonstrate the integration of complimentary and disparate pieces of medical informatics software. The Middleware software, as part of the larger Exploration Medical System, has potential training and simulation opportunities for future astronauts and ground personnel. In addition, the Exploration Medical System can serve as software infrastructure for future development and integration of medical devices and software.
<p>
RESULTS:<br>
The development, integration, and testing of all EMSD components - electronic medical record, assisted medical procedures software, Middleware infrastructure, and associated Middleware "adapters" were completed.
<p>
